{
  "version": 1,
  "mode": "behavior",
  "reason": "Config saves are compare-and-swap on every save path (save, save_resolved, missing-file defaults, acknowledged overwrite): a stale editor (another configurator, an external editor, a removal, a never-read path) never replaces a newer file. Clean, it adopts the newer file only if it resolves, and writes nothing; dirty, it reports the conflict, keeps its draft and offers reload (never writing defaults over a removed file, never accepting a newer file whose selected theme fails) or an acknowledged overwrite that keeps the exact replaced bytes in a backup no more readable than the source, never replacing or writing through an existing backup or symlink. Simultaneous saves of one version have one winner; conflict-free saves still reach the daemon's watch exactly once; TB-42's theme save block is preserved.",
  "files": [
    "crates/tb-config/tests/config_stale_save.rs",
    "crates/tb-config/tests/config_conflict_overwrite.rs",
    "crates/tb-config/tests/config_save.rs",
    "crates/tb-config/tests/config_watch.rs",
    "crates/tb-app/tests/configurator_conflict.rs",
    "crates/tb-app/tests/support/configurator.rs",
    "crates/tb-app/tests/support/ui.rs",
    "crates/tb-config/tests/config_save_resolved.rs"
  ],
